 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Four finite-level rectangle corners",
 "statement": "For the proper Cartesian square $\\square$, put $E=L(g')^*K$ and, for every\n$n\\geq1$, define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_n&:=Lg^*((Rf_*K)\\otimes^LP_n),&\nB_n&:=Lg^*Rf_*K_n,\\\\\nC_n&:=(Rf'_*E)\\otimes^LP_n,&\nD_n&:=Rf'_*E_n,\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $E_n=L(g')^*K_n=E\\otimes^LP_n$. The chosen Cartesian\nidentification supplies\n$L(g')^*Lf^*=L(f')^*Lg^*$ throughout.",
 "source": {
